 ### 3.5 Verification and validation hierarchy
 
-Code verification comprises analytic volume and hydrostatic checks, deck-point rigid-body transformations, action-reaction residuals, exact translational mass closure, platform energy balance, and numerical refinement. The repository regression comparator was also applied to the locally generated outputs for its four certification cases, using its registered 10% relative and (10^{-7}) absolute tolerances. It reports 157 file-level failures: 65 for Cylinder, 13 for DeepCwind, 7 for HywindSpar and 72 for Moonpool. The reason for these discrepancies has not been established, so the certification comparison is recorded as failed and provides no validation credit here. Submodel validation is consequently limited to the qualified parts of the Yang drop-test comparison; it does not validate the full-scale vehicle. Literature comparisons with Nargolkar, Wang and Xie are limited to coupling direction, forcing provenance and response trend. No public full-scale sea-touchdown experiment exists for the present barge-vehicle combination. The final calculation is therefore a numerical framework demonstration, not a validated full-scale predictor.
+Verification checks address different claims. Geometry and hydrostatic checks examine generated inputs; rigid-body tests examine coordinate transformations; algebraic reaction residuals examine wrench assembly; mass closure examines bookkeeping; and the platform energy ledger examines a specific discrete work balance. None alone validates a landing mechanism. The archived repository comparator reports 157 file-level failures at its registered 10% relative and \(10^{-7}\) absolute tolerances: 65 for Cylinder, 13 for DeepCwind, 7 for HywindSpar and 72 for Moonpool. Their cause is unresolved, so no solver-certification credit is taken.
+
+The independent review rebuilt the supplied Fortran source, ran the configured Cylinder case, and ran the medium barge at 0.6, 0.65, 0.775, 0.8 and 1.0 rad/s over seven headings. The selected diagonal hydrodynamic coefficients match the retained medium outputs at file precision, and principal motion amplitudes differ only at near-zero roundoff level. Other very small coupling entries are not bitwise identical. The fresh Cylinder comparison still shows a substantive damping discrepancy against the supplied benchmark, discussed with the detailed numerical evidence. These limited executions do not replace the missing full certification result.
+
+The review also independently integrated all three reduced drop-test cases, repeated the simultaneous-case fit, reconstructed 1000 random-phase records for one critical sea condition, and replayed the platform equation with archived contact forcing. Those are the reruns actually completed. PyChrono is absent from the review environment, so a fresh full-scale contact solve and the candidate corrections have not been dynamically verified here. No experimental dataset for the complete present barge-vehicle combination is supplied. Its full-scale use remains an unvalidated numerical example.
 
